---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ContentHero from '../components/ContentHero.astro';
import ContentBlock from '../components/ContentBlock.astro';
import RestorEmbed from '../components/RestorEmbed.astro';
import SiteSignup from '../components/SiteSignup.astro';
import TakeAction from '../components/TakeAction.astro';
import warleighHero from '../assets/pages/warleigh-nature-reserve/hero.jpg';
import warleighOne from '../assets/pages/warleigh-nature-reserve/warleigh-1.jpg';
import warleighTwo from '../assets/pages/warleigh-nature-reserve/warleigh-2.jpg';
import warleighThree from '../assets/pages/warleigh-nature-reserve/warleigh-3.jpg';
import warleighFour from '../assets/pages/warleigh-nature-reserve/warleigh-4.jpg';
---

<Layout
	title="Warleigh Nature Reserve"
	description="Restoring an 81-acre mosaic of wetland, woodland, and grassland between Bath and Bradford-on-Avon."
>
	<ContentHero
		title="Warleigh Nature Reserve"
		imgSrc={warleighHero}
		imgAlt="Warleigh Nature Reserve landscape by the River Avon"
	>
		<p>Warleigh Lane, Bathford, Bath</p>
		<p>
			Warleigh Nature Reserve is Protect Earth&apos;s 81-acre restoration site between Warleigh Wood
			and the River Avon. Together with volunteers and neighbours, we are restoring a rich mosaic of
			habitats for wildlife and people.
		</p>
	</ContentHero>

	<section class="page-sections wrap">
		<ContentBlock
			imgSrc={warleighOne}
			imgAlt="Volunteers and habitat at Warleigh Nature Reserve"
			title="From disused farmland to nature reserve"
		>
			<p>
				After two years of fundraising, legal work, and determination, Protect Earth completed the
				purchase of Warleigh in early 2026. The reserve now connects ancient woodland, wet meadow,
				wet woodland, coppice, scrub, and calcareous grassland in one linked landscape.
			</p>
			<p>
				Natural regeneration is already underway across the site, and the long-term vision is a more
				resilient, species-rich ecosystem that supports both biodiversity and local community
				access.
			</p>
		</ContentBlock>

		<ContentBlock
			imgSrc={warleighThree}
			imgAlt="Wetland and riverside habitat at Warleigh"
			title="What restoration work is happening now"
			isReversed
		>
			<p>
				The team and volunteers are already clearing old fencing, planting hedgerows to link up
				future woodlands, opening up access paths, restoring hazel coppice, tackling Himalayan
				balsam, and improving wet habitats with alder, willow, and leaky dams.
			</p>
			<p>
				These first steps are focused on helping wildlife recover quickly while setting up decades
				of care, including better conditions for species already seen on site like beavers and
				otters.
			</p>
		</ContentBlock>

		<ContentBlock
			imgSrc={warleighFour}
			imgAlt="Work party activity at Warleigh Nature Reserve"
			title="Support Warleigh's future"
		>
			<p>
				Buying the land was only the beginning. There is still a huge amount to fund, from practical
				conservation work and habitat recovery to safer access and long-term site management.
			</p>
			<p>
				If you want to help secure the future of this reserve, please donate to the crowdfunder.
				Every contribution goes directly into restoration work on the ground.
			</p>
			<div class="cta">
				<a
					href="https://www.crowdfunder.co.uk/p/warleigh-nature-reserve"
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener noreferrer"
					class="button"
				>
					Donate to Warleigh Crowdfunder
				</a>
			</div>
		</ContentBlock>

		<ContentBlock
			imgSrc={warleighTwo}
			imgAlt="Volunteer activity and access path at Warleigh Nature Reserve"
			title="Volunteer days at Warleigh"
			isReversed
		>
			<p>
				Warleigh runs regular volunteer work parties through spring and summer. We typically meet
				from 10:00 and finish around 16:00.
			</p>
			<p>See upcoming sessions and details on the events page.</p>
			<div class="cta">
				<a class="button" href="/events/warleigh-summer-work-parties-2026-e6rw8">
					View Warleigh volunteer days
				</a>
			</div>
		</ContentBlock>

		<section class="warleigh-location stack">
			<h2>Location</h2>
			<RestorEmbed
				url="https://restor.eco/embed/sites/5777be4d-85d0-4abd-bcb2-17b748bd20f6/"
				siteName="Warleigh Nature Reserve"
			/>
		</section>

		<SiteSignup
			title="Keep in the loop about Warleigh"
			intro="Sign up for updates from Warleigh Nature Reserve, including future work parties and restoration progress."
			site="warleigh_nature_reserve"
		/>

		<TakeAction />
	</section>

	<style>
		.warleigh-location {
			padding-block: var(--space-xl);
		}

		.warleigh-location h2 {
			font-size: var(--font-2xl);
			text-align: center;
			margin: 0;
		}

		.video-embed {
			overflow: hidden;
			aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
		}

		.video-embed iframe {
			inline-size: 100%;
			block-size: 100%;
			border: 0;
		}
	</style>
</Layout>
